You are a senior review consolidator. Multiple independent reviewers have scored the same generated code.
Synthesize their feedback into a single consensus review.

## Original Prompt

Write a TypeScript program
that performs CRUD operations on items in an Azure Cosmos DB NoSQL container:
1. Create a CosmosClient using endpoint and key
2. Create a database "TestDB" and container "Items" with partition key "/category"
3. Create an item with properties: id, category, name, quantity
4. Read the item back using item().read()
5. Query items where category equals "electronics" using parameterized query
6. Replace the item with updated quantity using item().replace()
7. Delete the item using item().delete()

Show required npm package and handle errors with appropriate status code checks.

## Individual Reviews

### Reviewer 1 (claude-opus-4.6)
```json
{
  "model": "claude-opus-4.6",
  "scores": {
    "criteria": [
      {
        "name": "Code Builds",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Code is syntactically correct TypeScript. Imports (CosmosClient, ErrorResponse, SqlQuerySpec) are valid @azure/cosmos exports. Type usage and async patterns are correct. Could not run tsc due to environment restrictions, but code analysis shows no compilation issues."
      },
      {
        "name": "Latest Package Versions",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "@azure/cosmos 4.9.3 is the latest stable version, confirmed via npm registry."
      },
      {
        "name": "Best Practices",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Uses key-based authentication (endpoint + key) instead of DefaultAzureCredential from @azure/identity. While the prompt requested key-based auth, best practice is identity-based auth. No resource cleanup/dispose pattern."
      },
      {
        "name": "Error Handling",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Custom assertStatus function checks response status codes. isCosmosError type guard with describeCosmosError provides error-specific messages for common HTTP status codes (401, 403, 404, 409, 429). Top-level catch handles both Cosmos errors and generic errors."
      },
      {
        "name": "Code Quality",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Clean, well-structured code with proper TypeScript typing (ItemDocument type, generic type parameters on SDK calls), good separation of concerns (helper functions for validation, error checking), and clear console output."
      },
      {
        "name": "Correct @azure/ Scoped Packages",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Only uses @azure/cosmos which is the correct scoped package. No deprecated unscoped packages."
      },
      {
        "name": "@azure/identity for Authentication",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Does not include @azure/identity as a dependency. Uses endpoint + key authentication via environment variables (COSMOS_KEY). The criterion requires identity-based auth with no account keys."
      },
      {
        "name": "Client Constructor with Endpoint and Credential",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Uses new CosmosClient({ endpoint, key }) instead of new CosmosClient(endpoint, credential). No credential object from @azure/identity is used."
      },
      {
        "name": "Async/Await Pattern",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "All asynchronous operations use async/await. Entry point uses async main() with .catch() handler. No .then()/.catch() chains or callback patterns."
      },
      {
        "name": "Pagination with for-await-of",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Query uses fetchAll() which collects all results into memory at once. Should use for-await-of iteration over the query iterator for proper pagination."
      },
      {
        "name": "LRO Pattern (beginXxx + pollUntilDone)",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "No long-running operations exist in Cosmos DB CRUD operations. This criterion is not applicable and passes by default."
      },
      {
        "name": "RestError Exception Handling",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Uses ErrorResponse from @azure/cosmos with 'code' property instead of RestError from @azure/core-rest-pipeline with 'statusCode'. While functional for Cosmos-specific errors, does not follow the standard RestError pattern."
      },
      {
        "name": "No Deprecated Packages",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "No deprecated or legacy Azure packages in package.json. All dependencies use current @azure/* track."
      },
      {
        "name": "Logging via @azure/logger",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Does not use @azure/logger or setLogLevel(). No SDK diagnostic logging is configured. Uses only console.log/console.error for application-level output."
      },
      {
        "name": "package.json with Correct Dependencies",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Has valid package.json with @azure/cosmos, tsconfig.json with strict mode, @types/node, and TypeScript 6.x. Missing @azure/identity is noted in its own criterion."
      },
      {
        "name": "@azure/cosmos npm package",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "package.json includes @azure/cosmos ^4.9.3 as a dependency."
      },
      {
        "name": "CosmosClient constructor with endpoint and key",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "new CosmosClient({ endpoint, key }) is used with values from environment variables."
      },
      {
        "name": "client.databases.createIfNotExists() and database.containers.createIfNotExists()",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Both methods are called correctly with appropriate parameters (database id, container id with partition key)."
      },
      {
        "name": "container.items.create(), container.item(id, partitionKey).read()",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "container.items.create\u003cItemDocument\u003e(item) and container.item(item.id, item.category).read\u003cItemDocument\u003e() are both present and correct."
      },
      {
        "name": "container.items.query() with SqlQuerySpec",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses container.items.query\u003cItemDocument\u003e(querySpec) with a properly typed SqlQuerySpec containing parameterized query and parameters array."
      },
      {
        "name": "container.item(id, partitionKey).replace() and .delete()",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Both itemRef.replace\u003cItemDocument\u003e(replacement) and itemRef.delete() are called correctly on the item reference."
      },
      {
        "name": "FeedResponse iteration and error status codes",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "fetchAll() returns FeedResponse with resources and statusCode. Status codes are checked via assertStatus for all operations including query (200), create (201), replace (200), delete (204)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "overall_score": 15,
  "max_score": 22,
  "summary": "The generated code is a well-structured TypeScript Cosmos DB CRUD sample that correctly implements all prompt-specific operations (create, read, query, replace, delete) with proper typing and status code validation. Main weaknesses are: uses key-based auth instead of @azure/identity, uses fetchAll() instead of for-await-of pagination, doesn't use RestError for exception handling, and lacks @azure/logger integration. Code quality and error handling are otherwise strong.",
  "issues": [
    "Uses key-based authentication (endpoint + key) instead of @azure/identity with DefaultAzureCredential",
    "Query uses fetchAll() instead of for-await-of iteration for proper pagination",
    "Error handling uses Cosmos ErrorResponse with 'code' instead of standard RestError with 'statusCode'",
    "No @azure/logger integration for SDK diagnostic logging",
    "Missing @azure/identity dependency entirely"
  ],
  "strengths": [
    "All 7 prompt-specific CRUD operations correctly implemented with proper SDK methods",
    "Strong custom error handling with status code assertions and Cosmos-specific error descriptions",
    "Clean TypeScript with proper type definitions (ItemDocument, generics on SDK calls)",
    "Environment variable validation with clear error messages",
    "Latest @azure/cosmos 4.9.3 package version",
    "Well-configured tsconfig.json with strict mode and modern target"
  ],
  "events": [
